            <div class="content-section">
                <div id="pgp-rise-tab1" class="content active">

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30 active hideFortheMENA " data-rel="tab-a-1">
                        <div class="left ">
                            <p class="faqHeading">How does the programme’s format support family business successors in driving change within their business? </p>

                            <img  src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer" id="tab-a-1">The PGP Rise:  Owners & Promoters Management is designed so that scions can apply their learnings to the business, in real time after each key module. The classes take place over the weekend, with learners having the option of attending them in person. </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-a-2">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">How does the curriculum address the unique challenges faced by family business owners?
                            </p>

                            <img  src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer" id="tab-a-2">The programme addresses the complete spectrum of responsibilities that family business owners must balance—family, business, self, and ownership. It also acknowledges the significance of including other key stakeholders in the process by conducting specialised “Extended Learning Sessions” for family members and the leadership team in dedicated residencies. </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-a-3">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">How does the programme implement a hands-on approach to solving business owners' challenges?
                            </p>

                            <img  src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer" id="tab-a-3">Alongside academic rigour, the programme encompasses a Capstone Project based on  real challenges faced by the learners in their family business. Over the course of 12 intensive months and with the help of 1:1 coaching with industry experts, learners will identify core challenges within the business and drive tangible solutions by the end of the programme.</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-a-4">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">How do international immersions and domestic residencies enhance the learning experience of participants?</p>

                            <img  src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer" id="tab-a-4">International immersions and domestic residencies offer a holistic learning experience, exposing learners to both global and local business perspectives. This diverse exposure enables learners to apply insights to their family enterprises, fostering their ability to navigate markets effectively.<br/>
                        Through <b>Global University Immersions</b>, participants are exposed to world-class practices and latest research equipping them with the tools to innovate and scale their family businesses internationally.The <b>Industrial Visits</b> allow them to understand global market trends, identify expansion opportunities and gain first-hand exposure to successful business models in international hubs. The <b>Domestic Residencies</b> offer a focused exploration of Indian family businesses, enabling participants to witness approaches that are unique to the Indian business landscape. 

                        
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-a-5">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">What will be the batch size of the class?</p>

                            <img  src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <div id="tab-a-5" class="faqanswer">
                            <p>We will limit the batch size to a maximum of 60 students to maximise individual attention from the masters and have an impactful teacher-student ratio.</p>

                            
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-a-6">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">What role does mentorship play in the overall learning experience of the programme?</p>

                            <img  src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg"
                                class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer" id="tab-a-6">Learners can expect 1:1 mentorship from experienced family business owners, industry titans & consultants, who provide firsthand insights drawn from their experiences in balancing family dynamics with business innovation. Additionally, many of our mentors hold CXO positions in multinational corporations, equipping learners with global best practices and strategies that can be directly applied to elevate their family enterprises. This blend of personal and global expertise ensures a comprehensive understanding of both family and business leadership. </p>
                    </div>

                    

                </div>

